Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Render named xcursor images at native physical resolution

Choose the nearest theme image to round(logical cursor size * output scale).
Upload at buffer scale 1 and render with physical geometry, rounding the
pointer-minus-hotspot origin once. Share this path with output and capture
rendering; retain client cursors, DnD and built-in fallback behaviour.
Bound decoded and texture caches by requested nominal size and keep animation
redraw selection in sync with the fractional size used for rendering.

Add size/cache tests and software-GLES pixel checks, including fractional
scales, clipping, non-nominal image dimensions and legacy fallback equivalence.

Generated with git diff b2aa8253; no commit or index mutation.
